# 1. Make decisions with PIOSEE

Date: 1992-01-12

## Status

Accepted

## Problem

Some of our decisions are made under pressure: what to do about an incident,
a failed release, a missed deadline or a supplier who has let us down. Made in
a hurry, in a call or a chat thread, such a decision is easily made on part
of the facts, by whoever spoke first, and is soon forgotten, along with what
was learned from it.

## Information

PIOSEE is a method of making a decision in six steps, taught to airline
pilots: Problem, Information, Options, Select, Execute and Evaluate. The
steps make the crew state the problem and the facts, stop them jumping to a
conclusion, give everyone a way to be heard, and make it normal to reverse a
decision that has not worked.

Its known weaknesses are that it can delay a quick, obvious action, that it
can be used to justify a decision rather than to make one, and that it does
not capture intuition.

See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilot_decision_making

## Options

* Carry on deciding as each situation demands, and recording nothing.
* Work through such decisions with PIOSEE, and record each one in this
  directory.
* Use a similar method, such as T-DODAR or FOR-DEC, which differ mostly in
  their words.

## Select

We will work through such decisions with PIOSEE, and record each one here,
so that the people making it see the same facts and options, and those who
come later can see what was known, what was weighed, what was done, and how
it turned out.

## Execute

* Each decision is a Markdown file in this directory, numbered in sequence.
  Numbers are not reused.
* Each has a section for each step of PIOSEE.
* A new record is a draft. Its status records what becomes of it.
* When harm is happening and the action that stops it is obvious, we act
  first, and record the decision afterwards.
* A record written after the event records the options considered at the
  time. What was seen only in hindsight belongs under Evaluate.
* A decision is evaluated once it has been carried out, in its own record. A
  decision that reverses an earlier one says so, and so does the decision it
  reverses. A decision that builds on an earlier one updates it, and both say
  so.

## Evaluate

To be evaluated once we have made a few decisions this way: whether the
records helped us decide, and whether anyone read them afterwards.
